Router replay (R3) for quantile-balancing routing.

Chonk's routers use quantile balancing (QB). QB picks the top-k experts itself and passes them to
topk_routing_with_score_function as precomputed_indices, which bypasses the RouterReplay hook there: with
moe_enable_routing_replay (NeMo RL policy.router_replay.enabled) the replayed vLLM routes were silently ignored.
TopKRouter._replay_qb_indices now applies RouterReplay to QB's picks through RouterReplay.get_replay_topk, the same
entry point as the top-k path: REPLAY_FORWARD / REPLAY_BACKWARD use the recorded rollout routes, RECORD records QB's
picks, no action leaves them unchanged. Wrappers of get_replay_topk (NeMo RL's fallback for tokens without rollout
routes) take QB's pick for such rows. The QB beta update still uses the forward's own scores.

